Package: ubuntu-passkey
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3,
         python3-cryptography,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-glib-2.0,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5),
         gir1.2-secret-1,
         polkitd | policykit-1,
         systemd,
         udev
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-ubuntu-passkey, gnome-keyring
Description: passkeys for Ubuntu (FIDO2 / WebAuthn authenticator)
 Ubuntu Passkey turns the computer into a FIDO2 security key, so passkeys can
 be created and used on websites in any browser without extra hardware.
 .
 It provides a per-user daemon that exposes a virtual USB security key through
 /dev/uhid, stores credentials encrypted with a key kept in the login keyring,
 verifies the user with their password or fingerprint through polkit, and the
 Passkeys application to manage stored passkeys.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-ubuntu-passkey
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 45), ubuntu-passkey (= ${binary:Version})
Description: GNOME Shell integration for Ubuntu Passkey
 Shows system-modal approval prompts in GNOME Shell when a website wants to
 create or use a passkey, and adds a Passkeys status menu to the top bar.
